Local patch for vendored social-auto-upload (see third_party/README.md).

Bilibili's upload path shells out to the external `biliup` binary, which
runtime.py downloads from GitHub on first use.  The upstream downloader only
talks to the GitHub Releases API, so an anonymous rate limit (HTTP 403) or a
network hiccup makes the very first B站 upload fail with no way to recover.

This patch makes the downloader resilient:
  - fall back to the release web page (whose 302 carries the latest tag) when
    the API is rate-limited or unreachable, since the page is not subject to
    the API's anonymous quota;
  - construct the asset URL from biliup's fixed release naming rules and
    confirm it with a HEAD request before downloading;
  - reuse an already-installed local biliup when the network is unavailable,
    instead of failing a publish that would otherwise have worked.

Applies to: uploader/bilibili_uploader/runtime.py and its unit test.

